<div class="px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <div class="sm:flex sm:items-center">
    <div class="sm:flex-auto">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Workouts</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">Sessions still to train, then the training already done.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 sm:ml-16 sm:mt-0 sm:flex-none">
      <a href="/workouts/new" type="button" class="<%= button_style %> block bg-lime-500 px-3 py-2 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 hover:bg-lime-600">New workout</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# The way in to the backfill's review list. #534.

      ## Why the doorway is here and not in the nav

      /workouts/withings has worked since #532 and nothing has ever linked to it, so the only
      way to reach it is to have just run `withings:backfill` with the output still on screen.
      A lifter who ran it, shut the terminal and came back on Sunday had no route to their own
      questions.

      The nav was the obvious home and is the wrong one. It is seven links on purpose, it
      already wraps to two rows between 640 and 840px, and an eighth would be carried on every
      page by every lifter -- including everyone who owns no watch -- to point at a screen
      that is empty except for the few days after a backfill. Making that entry conditional
      trades one problem for a worse one: people learn where things are by position, and a nav
      entry that comes and goes shifts every entry after it, so `settings` is fourth on
      Tuesday and fifth on Sunday.

      This page is where the questions already live. Every one of them is about a session in
      the list below, it is the page somebody opens when they sit down to deal with their
      training, and a line at the top of a page's own content is not a landmark anybody
      navigates by -- so it can appear and vanish without costing anyone their bearings. The
      screen's *permanent* address, the one that is the same whether or not anything is
      waiting, is the Withings block in settings, beside the connection that produces these
      questions in the first place.

      ## Why it says nothing when nothing is waiting

      Because there is nothing to say. This is a queue, not a destination: an empty one needs
      no door, and a line reading "no matches are waiting" would be the clutter the nav entry
      was rejected for, moved somewhere cheaper.

      ## The tint is the record page's, deliberately

      amber-50 inside a gray-300 border is exactly what `_withings_match` draws around the
      same question on a single session. The two screens are one queue seen from two angles,
      and a lifter who has answered one of these on a record should recognise this on sight as
      the same thing rather than read it as a second chore. %>
  <%- if @withings_waiting.positive? %>
    <div class="mt-4 rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-900">
        Your watch may have recorded <%= @withings_waiting %> of the sessions below.
        <a href="/workouts/withings" class="font-semibold underline">Say which are
          right</a> &mdash; or answer them one at a time on the sessions themselves.
      </p>
    </div>
  <%- end %>

  <%# Written sessions are only worth a heading of their own once there are some, so an
      account that has never generated a week sees the list it always saw. %>
  <%- unless @upcoming.empty? %>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Upcoming</h2>
    <%== render('workouts/_table', locals: { workouts: @upcoming }) %>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">History</h2>
  <%- end %>
  <%== render('workouts/_table', locals: { workouts: @workouts }) %>
</div>
